    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomObject> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        ADDED 2026-08-24. Logs each response received after materials go out at the Release
        Materials disposition stage - one row per response (a broker asking more questions,
        declining, or submitting an offer signal). Modelled on Counter_Offer__c (the child
        object behind lwc/loiCounterOffer), per explicit instruction: same minimal shape (no
        record types, no compact layout override, Private OWD, viewAllRecords=true in both
        disposition permission sets instead of a criteria/owner sharing rule), same AutoNumber
        Name convention, same Contact lookup-filter shape copied from a sibling.

        API NAME: Release_Materials_Response__c. Follows ARCHITECTURE.md Section 1
        (Title_Case_With_Underscores, no prefix) and the sibling child-log naming already in
        this module (Counter_Offer__c, BOV_Broker_Change__c) - a noun describing the row, not a
        verb. "Response" (singular per Salesforce object-naming convention, plural label
        pluralizes it) rather than "Log" - the object records the response itself, the same
        shape Counter_Offer__c takes for a single counter rather than being called
        "Counter_Log__c".

        UNLIKE Counter_Offer__c AND BOV_Broker_Change__c, THIS OBJECT IS HAND-ENTERED, NOT
        APEX-WRITTEN. Neither has an Apex service that stamps a response for a broker's inbound
        reply, and building one is out of scope for this declarative change (developer-agent
        territory, not requested). objectPermissions therefore grants allowCreate/allowEdit in
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit - unlike Counter_Offer__c/BOV_Broker_Change__c, which are
        deliberately allowCreate=false/allowEdit=false because Apex is their only writer. This
        is the same allowCreate=true shape NDA__c takes for the identical reason (D20/C2: a
        human must be able to click New).

        SETTINGS ARE COPIED FROM Counter_Offer__c.object-meta.xml, DELIBERATELY AND EXACTLY,
        matching every other disposition child object in this repo: sharingModel/
        externalSharingModel Private (the disposition module is uniformly Private OWD per the
        2026-07-22 RBAC build), enableHistory false, enableActivities false, enableReports
        true, enableSearch true, enableBulkApi true, enableStreamingApi true, deploymentStatus
        Deployed, visibility Public, compactLayoutAssignment SYSTEM (no custom compact layout -
        Counter_Offer__c ships none either and this object has too few fields to need one).
        AutoNumber name RMR-{0000} - checked against every <displayFormat> in this repo, free.

        🔴 FLS: EVERY FIELD ON THIS OBJECT ARRIVES WITH NO PERMISSIONS FOR ANYONE, SYSTEM
        ADMINISTRATOR INCLUDED, UNTIL THE PERMISSION SETS LAND. Read+edit is granted in
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit and read-only in DPEG_Disposition_View, in the same change, on
        all five custom fields (Method__c, Broker__c, Notes__c, Disposition__c,
        Entry_DateTime__c). This file, its fields, the layout, the empty sharing-rules
        placeholder and the two permission sets must land TOGETHER.

        🔴 SHARING: viewAllRecords=true in BOTH disposition permission sets (matching
        Counter_Offer__c exactly), so no sharingOwnerRules/sharingCriteriaRules entry is
        needed - an EMPTY placeholder sharingRules file ships instead, matching
        Counter_Offer__c's own empty file, kept only so a future rule has somewhere to land
        without creating a new file at that time.

        No record types: unlike NDA__c this object has exactly one shape and one purpose, so
        the record-type-scoped criteria-rule complexity NDA__c needed (D17) does not apply
        here - Counter_Offer__c is the correct, simpler precedent.
    -->
